WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.135
-My next guest is fresh
off her historic appearance

00:00:03.135 --> 00:00:05.805
at the Tokyo Olympics
where she won her sixth

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:09.008
individual gold medal
in swimming.

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:12.412
Ladies and gentlemen,
please welcome Katie Ledecky.

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:13.779
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.779 --> 00:00:15.448
-♪ Katie Ledecky ♪

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:17.884
♪ Do it for the win ♪

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.552
♪ Her gold medal ♪

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:21.721
♪ 'Cause she knows how to swim ♪

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.489
♪ Katie Ledecky ♪

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:25.591
♪ Sure as you can see ♪

00:00:25.591 --> 00:00:29.729
♪ After the Olympics
there's time for a trophy ♪

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:34.400
♪ Yeah! ♪

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:38.604
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:42.408 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:45.545
-That's the applause
you deserve, absolutely.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.480
Well, thank you so much
for coming on.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.248
Look at these medals.
-Yeah.

00:00:49.248 --> 00:00:50.783
-Oh, my goodness.
What does it --

00:00:50.783 --> 00:00:53.853
What does it feel like 'cause
now this is, what? 10?

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:56.755
-Yeah. Yeah. It's heavy.
-Yeah.

00:00:56.755 --> 00:00:58.858
-So I think I need
to give you one.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:01.261
You wanna wear one?
-Oh, I don't know.

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:03.796
Are you sure? Are you sure?
-What do you guys think? Yeah?

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:05.965
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.368
Yeah.
-This is amazing.

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:10.636
Wow. It is heavy.
-It's heavy.

00:01:10.636 --> 00:01:12.204
-Wait, but what --
this is like --

00:01:12.204 --> 00:01:13.205
can I do this?
-See, that's what we had

00:01:13.205 --> 00:01:14.574
to do in Tokyo.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:15.775
We had to present the medals
to ourselves.

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.476
So you're getting
the full experience.

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:18.811
-This feels like I was
in the Olympics.

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:20.746
This is unbelievable.
I've never done this before.

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:22.982
This is...

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:26.019
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.689 --> 00:01:33.192
Oh, my god.
This is unbelievable.

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:35.027
-Mm-hmm.
-Now, what...

00:01:35.027 --> 00:01:37.296
Out of all the medals you've won
do you have a favorite one?

00:01:37.296 --> 00:01:38.965
-I really like these.

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.700
The front is always the same.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:44.170
There's the event on the edge
all the time so.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.406
Let's see which event you won,
Jimmy.

00:01:47.406 --> 00:01:48.641
-Where is that?
Can you see that?

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.443
-You won the 800 meter
freestyle.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:51.811
-Do you have a close-up?

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.646
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.014
-I didn't know that that's...
[ speaks indistinctly ]

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:56.282
I was wondering.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.784
And then, what this side
is different.

00:01:58.784 --> 00:02:00.520
Was this side always the same?
-That side's always the same.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:03.189
Then the back Tokyo puts
their own little spin on it

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:04.958
so they put Tokyo 2020.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:07.493
-Holy moley.
-There you go.

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:09.962
-This is an honor to hold this.
Thank you so much.

00:02:09.962 --> 00:02:11.597
It's an honor to have you here.

00:02:11.597 --> 00:02:13.566
What was it like when
you were there, I mean,

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:17.837
no spectators, no family allowed
to come support you.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.605
What was it like?
-It was a little different.

00:02:19.605 --> 00:02:24.143
I'm lucky in that I had
my family there in 2012 and 2016

00:02:24.143 --> 00:02:26.312
so I had that experience.
-Sure.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.414
-But we missed an audience
like this, but...

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.015
-Of course.
-My teammates were in the stands

00:02:30.015 --> 00:02:32.218
cheering, the ones that
weren't racing each session.

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:34.820
And they really brought
some good energy so.

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:37.857
It didn't feel as weird
as I expected.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:40.760
-Online, I don't know if you
even look at what people say

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:45.331
about you but everyone's
calling you the GOAT of, yeah.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.633
Is it odd to be called that?

00:02:47.633 --> 00:02:50.035
-A little, I mean, there are
so many great swimmers

00:02:50.035 --> 00:02:51.471
throughout the years.

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:53.439
Of course Michael Phelps
is the GOAT

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:55.941
and I'm just honored
to carry on the legacy

00:02:55.941 --> 00:02:58.443
of really great female
swimmers in the US

00:02:58.443 --> 00:03:00.546
I don't know. Thanks.

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:02.715
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:04.383
-Speaking of Michael Phelps.
-Yes.

00:03:04.383 --> 00:03:07.586
-I have a photo here, this is
a picture of 9-year-old

00:03:07.586 --> 00:03:09.489
Katie Ledecky with
Michael Phelps.

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:12.992
Take a look at this.
Do you see this?

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:17.196
How cute is that? And did you --
he's just signing a --

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:18.797
was that a poster? Was he in
a band or something?

00:03:18.797 --> 00:03:21.567
-Yeah, it was at a swim clinic
so I had actually met him

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:23.369
and gotten his autograph
three years prior,

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:27.473
but I had to go to swim clinic
and get it again, I guess.

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:30.109
-Really?
-And, uh...

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:31.644
He's been such a great friend
over the years.

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.813
Six years after that photo,
I was on an Olympic team

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.114
with him in London.

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:36.849
He gave me a high-five
right before my race,

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:40.586
which made me flash back
to those moments and --

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:41.654
-That's amazing.

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:42.721
-He was there in Tokyo
supporting us

00:03:42.721 --> 00:03:44.657
and cheering us on
which was great.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:47.559
-I also heard that you were
a big fan of Bruce Springsteen.

00:03:47.559 --> 00:03:49.828
-Mm-hmm.
-And I have another photo.

00:03:49.828 --> 00:03:51.864
This is you and Bruce.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:54.567
Now what gold medal did he win?
I don't remember this.

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.035
-Oh, that would've been
either the 20 --

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:58.638
-Just rocking? Yeah.
-Yeah, from Rio.

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:01.440
-Did you see his daughter?
-Yes.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.709
She won a silver medal
in Tokyo.

00:04:03.709 --> 00:04:07.279
And it's funny because
when I showed him my medals

00:04:07.279 --> 00:04:11.150
he said, you know, my daughter
she's an equestrian

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.985
and it was really cool because
he was obviously

00:04:12.985 --> 00:04:15.121
very proud of his daughter
and I know that she had

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.856
Olympic potential so we really
followed her over

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:18.724
the last several years.

00:04:18.724 --> 00:04:20.359
And it was really cool to watch
her win a silver medal.

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:22.261
I mean, she's the boss.
-She won the freaking medal.

00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:24.030
-Yeah!
-Congratulations.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:27.332
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:27.332 --> 00:04:29.501
That's amazing.

00:04:29.501 --> 00:04:30.937
Okay, I want to ask you
a question that

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:32.671
I don't know if I've seen you
asked this before,

00:04:32.671 --> 00:04:38.010
but as a parent, I want to know,
can you eat before

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.912
you go in the pool?

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:41.647
Or do you have to wait
30 minutes

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:43.582
or is that real or --
let's get to it.

00:04:43.582 --> 00:04:44.984
I want a real fact here.

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:47.453
-I might have some parents
coming after me for this, but...

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:48.921
-Wow!

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:51.657
-I think we can debunk the myth.
You can eat before you swim.

00:04:51.657 --> 00:04:54.260
Not -- I wouldn't recommend
you go out and have a huge pizza

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:56.695
with your daughters before
you go for a swim.

00:04:56.695 --> 00:05:01.934
But I mean, I eat granola bars
before I swim within,

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.368
I don't know, five or 10 minutes
before I race.

00:05:03.368 --> 00:05:04.871
-I just hope my dad is watching
'cause this is...

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:06.739
-I drank a chocolate milk
right after I swim.

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:08.541
I sometimes have two races.

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:10.076
In Tokyo, I had two races
about an hour apart

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:13.512
and I was eating and drinking
and my second race

00:05:13.512 --> 00:05:16.783
was the 1,500 free so I had to
have something in my stomach to

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:19.118
get me through
a 15 1/2-minute race.

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:21.020
-I can't even tell you
what an honor it is

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.789
to have you on the show
and for representing

00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:24.090
our country.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.892
You're so cool
and an amazing athlete.

00:05:26.892 --> 00:05:28.528
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:28.528 --> 00:05:30.430
Please come back, will you?
-Thank you, yeah.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.130
-There you are right there,
Olympic champion,

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:34.200
Katie Ledecky, everybody.

